# No LCCC_NO_COMPARE here: GCC is a valid oracle for this test now.
#
# It used to be off. GCC's headers gate the 256-bit VAES/VPCLMULQDQ
# declarations behind __VAES__ / __VPCLMULQDQ__ (&& __AVX512F__ in the 12.x
# headers), so the flag set this test used to carry -- `-mavx2 -maes
# -mpclmul` -- could not compile the file with GCC at all: the 32-byte vector
# intrinsics were declared by lccc's bundled header only.
#
# The permission model then said what the instruction actually needs
# (`-mvaes`/`-mvpclmulqdq` plus the 256-bit vector class), and BOTH compilers
# accept the file under the flags in `.flags` (measured: gcc 12.2 accepts,
# lccc accepts), which is what makes the comparison meaningful: the oracle now
# builds the same 256-bit VAES/VPCLMULQDQ code and the outputs are compared.
